// This file is a fixture for testing envelope unwrapping in JSONL parsers.
//
// TOTAL LINES: 8
//
// STRUCTURE:
// Each line is a JSON object with an "envelope" structure:
// {
//   "type": "<event_type>",
//   "timestamp": "<ISO 8601 timestamp>",
//   "payload": { <event-specific data> }
// }
//
// The envelope has three top-level fields:
// - type: Event type discriminator (used for routing)
// - timestamp: When the event occurred (envelope-level metadata)
// - payload: Nested object containing the actual event data
//
// EVENT TYPES (8 total, 5 unique types):
// 1. session_start (line 1): Session initialization with metadata
//    - payload contains: session_id, model, cwd, role, content
//
// 2. heartbeat (line 2): Health check event
//    - payload contains: status, role, content
//
// 3. ping (line 3): Keepalive event
//    - payload contains: seq, role, content
//
// 4. message (lines 4-7): Conversation events (user/assistant/tool_call)
//    - payload contains: role, content
//    - tool_call events (line 6) additionally have: tool_name
//
// 5. unknown_event (line 8): Edge case for unexpected event types
//    - payload contains: data (extra field), role, content
//
// PAYLOAD PATTERNS:
// - Common fields in payload: role, content
// - role values observed: system, user, assistant, tool_call
// - Tool-specific data: tool_name field appears in tool_call events
// - Session metadata: session_id, model, cwd appear in session_start
// - Variable fields: Different event types have different additional fields
//
// USAGE:
// This fixture tests the envelope unwrapping feature where:
// 1. The parser extracts type and timestamp from the envelope level
// 2. The payload object becomes the event body for field mapping
// 3. Type-based routing determines how each event is processed
// 4. Field mapping can address envelope-level fields with ^ prefix (e.g., ^timestamp)
{"type": "session_start", "timestamp": "2026-07-04T10:00:00Z", "payload": {"session_id": "env-test-001", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "cwd": "/home/user/project", "role": "system", "content": "Session starting"}}
{"type": "heartbeat", "timestamp": "2026-07-04T10:00:05Z", "payload": {"status": "ok", "role": "system", "content": "Heartbeat"}}
{"type": "ping", "timestamp": "2026-07-04T10:00:10Z", "payload": {"seq": 1, "role": "system", "content": "Ping"}}
{"type": "message", "timestamp": "2026-07-04T10:00:15Z", "payload": {"role": "user", "content": "Refactor the authentication module to use JWT tokens"}}
{"type": "message", "timestamp": "2026-07-04T10:00:20Z", "payload": {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll refactor the authentication module. Let me start by reading the current implementation."}}
{"type": "message", "timestamp": "2026-07-04T10:00:25Z", "payload": {"role": "tool_call", "content": "Reading src/auth/mod.rs", "tool_name": "Read"}}
{"type": "message", "timestamp": "2026-07-04T10:00:30Z", "payload": {"role": "assistant", "content": "Here's the refactored authentication module using JWT."}}
{"type": "unknown_event", "timestamp": "2026-07-04T10:00:35Z", "payload": {"data": "something unexpected", "role": "system", "content": "Unknown event"}}
